IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg9-xi-receivers`

-- Tests of dg9-xi-receivers.l4 (8 Del. C. sections 291 to 303).
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text, beside the assertion, before the run.
-- The wrappers `t ...` only give a rule's inputs short positional names; they restate no rule.

§ `Test wrappers`

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 294 Inventory`
`t 294 inventory` a b c d e MEANS
    `s 294 Inventory` WITH `itemized inventory of all the assets of the corporation` IS a, `statement of the nature of the assets` IS b, `statement of the probable value of the assets` IS c, `account of all debts due from the corporation` IS d, `account of all debts due to the corporation` IS e

GIVEN insolvent IS A BOOLEAN
      who IS AN Actor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`t 291 applicant` insolvent who MEANS
    `s 291 the Court of Chancery may act on the application to appoint receivers for the insolvent corporation` WITH `the corporation is insolvent` IS insolvent, `the applicant` IS who

§ `s 291 Receivers for insolvent corporations`

-- Insolvent corporation; a creditor or a stockholder applies.
#ASSERT `t 291 applicant` TRUE `a creditor`
#ASSERT `t 291 applicant` TRUE `a stockholder`
-- A director, an officer or a stranger is not named by the section.
#ASSERT NOT (`t 291 applicant` TRUE `a director`)
#ASSERT NOT (`t 291 applicant` TRUE `an officer`)
#ASSERT NOT (`t 291 applicant` TRUE (`another party named in the provision` "a customer"))
-- Not insolvent: no application lies.
#ASSERT NOT (`t 291 applicant` FALSE `a creditor`)
-- The five powers.
#ASSERT `s 291 the receivers have the power` WITH `the power` IS `to take charge of the assets, estate, effects, business and affairs of the corporation`
#ASSERT `s 291 the receivers have the power` WITH `the power` IS `to collect the outstanding debts, claims, and property due and belonging to the corporation`
#ASSERT `s 291 the receivers have the power` WITH `the power` IS `to prosecute and defend, in the name of the corporation or otherwise, all claims or suits`
#ASSERT `s 291 the receivers have the power` WITH `the power` IS `to appoint an agent or agents under the receivers`
#ASSERT `s 291 the receivers have the power` WITH `the power` IS `to do all other acts which might be done by the corporation and which may be necessary or proper`
#ASSERT (count `s 291 the powers of the receivers`) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `s 291 the powers of the receivers continue` WITH `the Court of Chancery deems the continuation of the powers necessary` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 291 the powers of the receivers continue` WITH `the Court of Chancery deems the continuation of the powers necessary` IS FALSE)

§ `s 292 Title to property; filing order of appointment; exception`

-- Appointed by the Court, qualified, not pendente lite, the property not real estate outside this State: title vests.
#ASSERT `s 292(a) title of the corporation to the property is vested in the trustees or receivers by operation of law` WITH `the trustees or receivers were appointed by the Court of Chancery` IS TRUE, `the trustees or receivers are receivers appointed pendente lite` IS FALSE, `the trustees or receivers have been appointed and have qualified, or a co-trustee or co-receiver has died, resigned or been discharged` IS TRUE, `the property is real estate situate outside this State` IS FALSE
-- Receivers pendente lite: the section does not apply (subsection (c)).
#ASSERT NOT (`s 292(a) title of the corporation to the property is vested in the trustees or receivers by operation of law` WITH `the trustees or receivers were appointed by the Court of Chancery` IS TRUE, `the trustees or receivers are receivers appointed pendente lite` IS TRUE, `the trustees or receivers have been appointed and have qualified, or a co-trustee or co-receiver has died, resigned or been discharged` IS TRUE, `the property is real estate situate outside this State` IS FALSE)
-- Real estate outside this State is excepted.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 292(a) title of the corporation to the property is vested in the trustees or receivers by operation of law` WITH `the trustees or receivers were appointed by the Court of Chancery` IS TRUE, `the trustees or receivers are receivers appointed pendente lite` IS FALSE, `the trustees or receivers have been appointed and have qualified, or a co-trustee or co-receiver has died, resigned or been discharged` IS TRUE, `the property is real estate situate outside this State` IS TRUE)
-- Not yet qualified; not appointed by the Court.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 292(a) title of the corporation to the property is vested in the trustees or receivers by operation of law` WITH `the trustees or receivers were appointed by the Court of Chancery` IS TRUE, `the trustees or receivers are receivers appointed pendente lite` IS FALSE, `the trustees or receivers have been appointed and have qualified, or a co-trustee or co-receiver has died, resigned or been discharged` IS FALSE, `the property is real estate situate outside this State` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 292(a) title of the corporation to the property is vested in the trustees or receivers by operation of law` WITH `the trustees or receivers were appointed by the Court of Chancery` IS FALSE, `the trustees or receivers are receivers appointed pendente lite` IS FALSE, `the trustees or receivers have been appointed and have qualified, or a co-trustee or co-receiver has died, resigned or been discharged` IS TRUE, `the property is real estate situate outside this State` IS FALSE)
-- (b): a filing is required in each county where real estate belonging to the corporation is situated, but not by receivers pendente lite.
#ASSERT `s 292(b) the trustees or receivers must file a certified copy of the order of appointment and evidence of qualification in the office of the recorder of the county` WITH `the trustees or receivers were appointed by the Court of Chancery` IS TRUE, `the trustees or receivers are receivers appointed pendente lite` IS FALSE, `real estate belonging to the corporation is situated in the county` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 292(b) the trustees or receivers must file a certified copy of the order of appointment and evidence of qualification in the office of the recorder of the county` WITH `the trustees or receivers were appointed by the Court of Chancery` IS TRUE, `the trustees or receivers are receivers appointed pendente lite` IS FALSE, `real estate belonging to the corporation is situated in the county` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 292(b) the trustees or receivers must file a certified copy of the order of appointment and evidence of qualification in the office of the recorder of the county` WITH `the trustees or receivers were appointed by the Court of Chancery` IS TRUE, `the trustees or receivers are receivers appointed pendente lite` IS TRUE, `real estate belonging to the corporation is situated in the county` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 292(b) the trustees or receivers must file a certified copy of the order of appointment and evidence of qualification in the office of the recorder of the county` WITH `the trustees or receivers were appointed by the Court of Chancery` IS FALSE, `the trustees or receivers are receivers appointed pendente lite` IS FALSE, `real estate belonging to the corporation is situated in the county` IS TRUE)
-- 20 days from the date of qualification (1 March 2026): the 20th day is 21 March 2026.
#ASSERT (`s 292(b) the time after qualification to file in the office of the recorder`)'s `how many units` EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `s 292(b) the filing in the office of the recorder was made in time` WITH `the date of their qualification` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 1, `the date they filed in the office of the recorder of the county, if they did` IS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 21)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 292(b) the filing in the office of the recorder was made in time` WITH `the date of their qualification` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 1, `the date they filed in the office of the recorder of the county, if they did` IS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 22))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 292(b) the filing in the office of the recorder was made in time` WITH `the date of their qualification` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 1, `the date they filed in the office of the recorder of the county, if they did` IS NOTHING)

§ `s 293 to s 295 notices, inventory, proofs of claim`

-- s 293: the Register in Chancery gives the notices, unless the Court orders otherwise.
#ASSERT `s 293 the notice is to be given by the Register in Chancery` WITH `a notice is required to be given to stockholders and creditors in an action in which a receiver or trustee for the corporation was appointed` IS TRUE, `the Court of Chancery has ordered that the notice be given otherwise` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 293 the notice is to be given by the Register in Chancery` WITH `a notice is required to be given to stockholders and creditors in an action in which a receiver or trustee for the corporation was appointed` IS TRUE, `the Court of Chancery has ordered that the notice be given otherwise` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 293 the notice is to be given by the Register in Chancery` WITH `a notice is required to be given to stockholders and creditors in an action in which a receiver or trustee for the corporation was appointed` IS FALSE, `the Court of Chancery has ordered that the notice be given otherwise` IS FALSE)
-- s 294: a full and complete itemized inventory filed with the Register in Chancery.
--  columns of the inventory: itemized inventory, nature, probable value, debts due from, debts due to
#ASSERT `s 294 the inventory is full and complete and filed as the section requires` WITH `the inventory` IS (`t 294 inventory` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE), `the inventory is filed in the office of the Register in Chancery of the county in which the proceeding is pending` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 294 the inventory is full and complete and filed as the section requires` WITH `the inventory` IS (`t 294 inventory` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE), `the inventory is filed in the office of the Register in Chancery of the county in which the proceeding is pending` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 294 the inventory is full and complete and filed as the section requires` WITH `the inventory` IS (`t 294 inventory` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE), `the inventory is filed in the office of the Register in Chancery of the county in which the proceeding is pending` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 294 the inventory is full and complete and filed as the section requires` WITH `the inventory` IS (`t 294 inventory` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE), `the inventory is filed in the office of the Register in Chancery of the county in which the proceeding is pending` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 294 the inventory is full and complete and filed as the section requires` WITH `the inventory` IS (`t 294 inventory` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE), `the inventory is filed in the office of the Register in Chancery of the county in which the proceeding is pending` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 294 the inventory is full and complete and filed as the section requires` WITH `the inventory` IS (`t 294 inventory` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE), `the inventory is filed in the office of the Register in Chancery of the county in which the proceeding is pending` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 294 the inventory is full and complete and filed as the section requires` WITH `the inventory` IS (`t 294 inventory` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE), `the inventory is filed in the office of the Register in Chancery of the county in which the proceeding is pending` IS FALSE)
-- The report to the Court is due when, and as often as, the Court directs.
#ASSERT `s 294 the trustees or receivers must make a report to the Court of their proceedings` WITH `the Court of Chancery has directed a report on this occasion` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 294 the trustees or receivers must make a report to the Court of their proceedings` WITH `the Court of Chancery has directed a report on this occasion` IS FALSE)
-- s 295: proof under oath, filed in time (the last day fixed is 30 June 2026).
#ASSERT `s 295 the creditor has made and filed proof of the claim as the section requires` WITH `the creditor made proof of the claim under oath` IS TRUE, `the creditor caused the proof to be filed in the office of the Register in Chancery of the county in which the proceeding is pending` IS TRUE, `the date the proof was filed` IS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30), `the last day fixed for filing proofs of claim by the rules of the Court of Chancery or the order of the Court` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 30
#ASSERT NOT (`s 295 the creditor has made and filed proof of the claim as the section requires` WITH `the creditor made proof of the claim under oath` IS TRUE, `the creditor caused the proof to be filed in the office of the Register in Chancery of the county in which the proceeding is pending` IS TRUE, `the date the proof was filed` IS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1), `the last day fixed for filing proofs of claim by the rules of the Court of Chancery or the order of the Court` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 30)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 295 the creditor has made and filed proof of the claim as the section requires` WITH `the creditor made proof of the claim under oath` IS TRUE, `the creditor caused the proof to be filed in the office of the Register in Chancery of the county in which the proceeding is pending` IS TRUE, `the date the proof was filed` IS NOTHING, `the last day fixed for filing proofs of claim by the rules of the Court of Chancery or the order of the Court` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 30)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 295 the creditor has made and filed proof of the claim as the section requires` WITH `the creditor made proof of the claim under oath` IS FALSE, `the creditor caused the proof to be filed in the office of the Register in Chancery of the county in which the proceeding is pending` IS TRUE, `the date the proof was filed` IS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1), `the last day fixed for filing proofs of claim by the rules of the Court of Chancery or the order of the Court` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 30)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 295 the creditor has made and filed proof of the claim as the section requires` WITH `the creditor made proof of the claim under oath` IS TRUE, `the creditor caused the proof to be filed in the office of the Register in Chancery of the county in which the proceeding is pending` IS FALSE, `the date the proof was filed` IS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1), `the last day fixed for filing proofs of claim by the rules of the Court of Chancery or the order of the Court` IS YearMonthDay 2026 6 30)
-- The bar comes only by the Court's direction.
#ASSERT (`s 295 the creditor is barred from participating in the distribution of the assets` WITH `the creditor has made and filed proof of the claim as section 295 requires` IS FALSE, `the Court of Chancery has directed that the creditor be barred from participating in the distribution` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Failed to prove in time, but the Court has not directed: not yet barred and not safe either, so not covered.
#ASSERT (`s 295 the creditor is barred from participating in the distribution of the assets` WITH `the creditor has made and filed proof of the claim as section 295 requires` IS FALSE, `the Court of Chancery has directed that the creditor be barred from participating in the distribution` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 295 the creditor is barred from participating in the distribution of the assets` WITH `the creditor has made and filed proof of the claim as section 295 requires` IS TRUE, `the Court of Chancery has directed that the creditor be barred from participating in the distribution` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The notice the Court prescribed.
#ASSERT `s 295 the creditors have been given the notice the Court of Chancery prescribed` WITH `the Court of Chancery has prescribed what notice, by publication or otherwise, is to be given to the creditors of the time fixed` IS TRUE, `the prescribed notice has been given to the creditors` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 295 the creditors have been given the notice the Court of Chancery prescribed` WITH `the Court of Chancery has prescribed what notice, by publication or otherwise, is to be given to the creditors of the time fixed` IS TRUE, `the prescribed notice has been given to the creditors` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 295 the creditors have been given the notice the Court of Chancery prescribed` WITH `the Court of Chancery has prescribed what notice, by publication or otherwise, is to be given to the creditors of the time fixed` IS FALSE, `the prescribed notice has been given to the creditors` IS FALSE

§ `s 296 Adjudication of claims; appeal`

-- Notice received 1 March 2026: the 30th day is 31 March 2026.
#ASSERT (`s 296(a) the time after the notice to inspect the claims`)'s `how many units` EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `s 296(a) the claims were inspected within 30 days after the notice` WITH `the date the trustee or receiver received the Register's notice of the filing of the claims` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 1, `the date the trustee or receiver inspected the claims` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 31
#ASSERT NOT (`s 296(a) the claims were inspected within 30 days after the notice` WITH `the date the trustee or receiver received the Register's notice of the filing of the claims` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 1, `the date the trustee or receiver inspected the claims` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 1)
-- A claim disputed by the trustee or receiver, or by any creditor: the creditor whose claim is disputed is notified forthwith.
#ASSERT `s 296(a) the trustee or receiver must forthwith notify the creditor whose claim is disputed of the decision` WITH `the trustee or receiver is not satisfied with the validity or correctness of the claim` IS TRUE, `a creditor is not satisfied with the validity or correctness of the claim` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 296(a) the trustee or receiver must forthwith notify the creditor whose claim is disputed of the decision` WITH `the trustee or receiver is not satisfied with the validity or correctness of the claim` IS FALSE, `a creditor is not satisfied with the validity or correctness of the claim` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 296(a) the trustee or receiver must forthwith notify the creditor whose claim is disputed of the decision` WITH `the trustee or receiver is not satisfied with the validity or correctness of the claim` IS FALSE, `a creditor is not satisfied with the validity or correctness of the claim` IS FALSE)
-- The disputing creditor submits to the examination the trustee or receiver directs and produces the books and papers required.
#ASSERT `s 296(a) the creditor whose claim is disputed must submit to the examination` WITH `the creditor’s claim is disputed` IS TRUE, `the trustee or receiver has directed an examination in relation to the claim` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 296(a) the creditor whose claim is disputed must submit to the examination` WITH `the creditor’s claim is disputed` IS FALSE, `the trustee or receiver has directed an examination in relation to the claim` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 296(a) the creditor whose claim is disputed must submit to the examination` WITH `the creditor’s claim is disputed` IS TRUE, `the trustee or receiver has directed an examination in relation to the claim` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 296(a) the creditor whose claim is disputed must produce the books and papers required` WITH `the creditor’s claim is disputed` IS TRUE, `the trustee or receiver has required the production of books and papers relating to the claim` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 296(a) the creditor whose claim is disputed must produce the books and papers required` WITH `the creditor’s claim is disputed` IS FALSE, `the trustee or receiver has required the production of books and papers relating to the claim` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 296(a) the creditor whose claim is disputed must produce the books and papers required` WITH `the creditor’s claim is disputed` IS TRUE, `the trustee or receiver has required the production of books and papers relating to the claim` IS FALSE)
-- The three powers and duties on the claims.
#ASSERT `s 296(a) the trustee or receiver has the power or duty on the claims` WITH `the power or duty` IS `to examine, under oath or affirmation, all witnesses produced before the trustee or receiver touching the claims`
#ASSERT `s 296(a) the trustee or receiver has the power or duty on the claims` WITH `the power or duty` IS `to pass upon and allow or disallow the claims, or any part of them`
#ASSERT `s 296(a) the trustee or receiver has the power or duty on the claims` WITH `the power or duty` IS `to notify the claimants of the determination`
-- (b): appeal within 30 days after receiving notice of disallowance (received 1 March 2026: last day 31 March 2026).
#ASSERT (`s 296(b) the time after the notice of disallowance to appeal`)'s `how many units` EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `s 296(b) the creditor or claimant may appeal to the Court of Chancery` WITH `the creditor or claimant received notice from the receiver or trustee that the claim has been disallowed in whole or in part` IS TRUE, `the date the creditor or claimant received the notice` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 1, `the date the creditor or claimant appeals to the Court of Chancery` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 31
#ASSERT NOT (`s 296(b) the creditor or claimant may appeal to the Court of Chancery` WITH `the creditor or claimant received notice from the receiver or trustee that the claim has been disallowed in whole or in part` IS TRUE, `the date the creditor or claimant received the notice` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 1, `the date the creditor or claimant appeals to the Court of Chancery` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 296(b) the creditor or claimant may appeal to the Court of Chancery` WITH `the creditor or claimant received notice from the receiver or trustee that the claim has been disallowed in whole or in part` IS FALSE, `the date the creditor or claimant received the notice` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 1, `the date the creditor or claimant appeals to the Court of Chancery` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 15)

§ `s 297 to s 299 sale of perishable property, compensation, substitution`

#ASSERT `s 297 the Court of Chancery may order the receiver or trustee to sell the property clear of all encumbrances` WITH `the property of the corporation is encumbered with liens of any character at the time of the appointment of the receiver or trustee` IS TRUE, `the validity, extent or legality of a lien is disputed or brought in question` IS TRUE, `the property is of a character which will deteriorate in value pending the litigation respecting the lien` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 297 the Court of Chancery may order the receiver or trustee to sell the property clear of all encumbrances` WITH `the property of the corporation is encumbered with liens of any character at the time of the appointment of the receiver or trustee` IS FALSE, `the validity, extent or legality of a lien is disputed or brought in question` IS TRUE, `the property is of a character which will deteriorate in value pending the litigation respecting the lien` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 297 the Court of Chancery may order the receiver or trustee to sell the property clear of all encumbrances` WITH `the property of the corporation is encumbered with liens of any character at the time of the appointment of the receiver or trustee` IS TRUE, `the validity, extent or legality of a lien is disputed or brought in question` IS FALSE, `the property is of a character which will deteriorate in value pending the litigation respecting the lien` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 297 the Court of Chancery may order the receiver or trustee to sell the property clear of all encumbrances` WITH `the property of the corporation is encumbered with liens of any character at the time of the appointment of the receiver or trustee` IS TRUE, `the validity, extent or legality of a lien is disputed or brought in question` IS TRUE, `the property is of a character which will deteriorate in value pending the litigation respecting the lien` IS FALSE)
-- A price of 1000 less costs of the sale of 120 pays 880 into the Court.
#ASSERT (`s 297 the net proceeds paid into the Court` WITH `the price obtained for the property` IS 1000, `the costs of the sale` IS 120) EQUALS 880
-- s 298: charges first. Assets 1000 less compensation 100, costs and expenses 50 and costs of proceedings 25 leave 825.
#ASSERT (`s 298 the assets left for distribution among the creditors or stockholders` WITH `the assets of the corporation` IS 1000, `the compensation the Court of Chancery allows the receiver or trustee` IS 100, `the costs and expenses incurred in and about the execution of the trust` IS 50, `the costs of the proceedings in the Court` IS 25) EQUALS JUST 825
-- Assets exactly equal to the charges (175) leave nothing; 174 is less than the charges: not covered.
#ASSERT (`s 298 the assets left for distribution among the creditors or stockholders` WITH `the assets of the corporation` IS 175, `the compensation the Court of Chancery allows the receiver or trustee` IS 100, `the costs and expenses incurred in and about the execution of the trust` IS 50, `the costs of the proceedings in the Court` IS 25) EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT (`s 298 the assets left for distribution among the creditors or stockholders` WITH `the assets of the corporation` IS 174, `the compensation the Court of Chancery allows the receiver or trustee` IS 100, `the costs and expenses incurred in and about the execution of the trust` IS 50, `the costs of the proceedings in the Court` IS 25) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 299: substitution as party plaintiff.
#ASSERT `s 299 the trustee or receiver is substituted as party plaintiff in the place of the corporation` WITH `the trustee or receiver has applied in the court in which the suit is pending` IS TRUE, `the corporation is the plaintiff in the suit or proceeding` IS TRUE, `the suit or proceeding was pending at the time of the trustee’s or receiver’s appointment` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 299 the trustee or receiver is substituted as party plaintiff in the place of the corporation` WITH `the trustee or receiver has applied in the court in which the suit is pending` IS FALSE, `the corporation is the plaintiff in the suit or proceeding` IS TRUE, `the suit or proceeding was pending at the time of the trustee’s or receiver’s appointment` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 299 the trustee or receiver is substituted as party plaintiff in the place of the corporation` WITH `the trustee or receiver has applied in the court in which the suit is pending` IS TRUE, `the corporation is the plaintiff in the suit or proceeding` IS FALSE, `the suit or proceeding was pending at the time of the trustee’s or receiver’s appointment` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 299 the trustee or receiver is substituted as party plaintiff in the place of the corporation` WITH `the trustee or receiver has applied in the court in which the suit is pending` IS TRUE, `the corporation is the plaintiff in the suit or proceeding` IS TRUE, `the suit or proceeding was pending at the time of the trustee’s or receiver’s appointment` IS FALSE)
-- An action against a trustee or receiver who has died: on suggestion of the facts it continues against the successor, or the corporation if there is none.
#ASSERT (`s 299 the action against the trustee or receiver, who has died, continues against` WITH `the facts have been suggested on the record` IS TRUE, `a new trustee or receiver has been appointed` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST `the successor of the trustee or receiver`
#ASSERT (`s 299 the action against the trustee or receiver, who has died, continues against` WITH `the facts have been suggested on the record` IS TRUE, `a new trustee or receiver has been appointed` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the corporation`
#ASSERT (`s 299 the action against the trustee or receiver, who has died, continues against` WITH `the facts have been suggested on the record` IS FALSE, `a new trustee or receiver has been appointed` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 300 Employee’s lien for wages when corporation insolvent`

-- A person in the regular employ of an insolvent corporation of this State, not an officer, has the lien.
#ASSERT `s 300 the person has a lien upon the assets of the corporation for wages, paid prior to any other debt` WITH `the corporation is a corporation of this State or a foreign corporation doing business in this State` IS TRUE, `the corporation has become insolvent` IS TRUE, `the person does labor or service of whatever character in the regular employ of the corporation` IS TRUE, `the person is an officer of the corporation` IS FALSE
-- "The word 'employee' shall not be construed to include any of the officers of the corporation."
#ASSERT NOT (`s 300 the person has a lien upon the assets of the corporation for wages, paid prior to any other debt` WITH `the corporation is a corporation of this State or a foreign corporation doing business in this State` IS TRUE, `the corporation has become insolvent` IS TRUE, `the person does labor or service of whatever character in the regular employ of the corporation` IS TRUE, `the person is an officer of the corporation` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 300 the person has a lien upon the assets of the corporation for wages, paid prior to any other debt` WITH `the corporation is a corporation of this State or a foreign corporation doing business in this State` IS TRUE, `the corporation has become insolvent` IS FALSE, `the person does labor or service of whatever character in the regular employ of the corporation` IS TRUE, `the person is an officer of the corporation` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 300 the person has a lien upon the assets of the corporation for wages, paid prior to any other debt` WITH `the corporation is a corporation of this State or a foreign corporation doing business in this State` IS TRUE, `the corporation has become insolvent` IS TRUE, `the person does labor or service of whatever character in the regular employ of the corporation` IS FALSE, `the person is an officer of the corporation` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 300 the person has a lien upon the assets of the corporation for wages, paid prior to any other debt` WITH `the corporation is a corporation of this State or a foreign corporation doing business in this State` IS FALSE, `the corporation has become insolvent` IS TRUE, `the person does labor or service of whatever character in the regular employ of the corporation` IS TRUE, `the person is an officer of the corporation` IS FALSE)
-- "not exceeding 2 months' wages": with a month's wages of 2000 the lien is at most 4000.
#ASSERT `s 300 the months of wages the lien does not exceed` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT (`s 300 the amount of the lien for wages` WITH `the person has a lien under section 300` IS TRUE, `the wages due to the person` IS 5000, `the person's wages for one month` IS 2000) EQUALS 4000
#ASSERT (`s 300 the amount of the lien for wages` WITH `the person has a lien under section 300` IS TRUE, `the wages due to the person` IS 3999, `the person's wages for one month` IS 2000) EQUALS 3999
#ASSERT (`s 300 the amount of the lien for wages` WITH `the person has a lien under section 300` IS TRUE, `the wages due to the person` IS 4000, `the person's wages for one month` IS 2000) EQUALS 4000
#ASSERT (`s 300 the amount of the lien for wages` WITH `the person has a lien under section 300` IS TRUE, `the wages due to the person` IS 4001, `the person's wages for one month` IS 2000) EQUALS 4000
-- No lien: nothing.
#ASSERT (`s 300 the amount of the lien for wages` WITH `the person has a lien under section 300` IS FALSE, `the wages due to the person` IS 5000, `the person's wages for one month` IS 2000) EQUALS 0

§ `s 301 Discontinuance of liquidation`

#ASSERT `s 301 the liquidation of the assets and business of the insolvent corporation may be discontinued` WITH `it is established that cause for liquidation no longer exists` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 301 the liquidation of the assets and business of the insolvent corporation may be discontinued` WITH `it is established that cause for liquidation no longer exists` IS FALSE)
-- Redelivery needs the Court's order as well as the cause having ended.
#ASSERT `s 301 the receiver or trustee must redeliver to the corporation all of its remaining property and assets` WITH `it is established that cause for liquidation no longer exists` IS TRUE, `the Court of Chancery, in its discretion, dismisses the proceedings and directs the redelivery` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 301 the receiver or trustee must redeliver to the corporation all of its remaining property and assets` WITH `it is established that cause for liquidation no longer exists` IS TRUE, `the Court of Chancery, in its discretion, dismisses the proceedings and directs the redelivery` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 301 the receiver or trustee must redeliver to the corporation all of its remaining property and assets` WITH `it is established that cause for liquidation no longer exists` IS FALSE, `the Court of Chancery, in its discretion, dismisses the proceedings and directs the redelivery` IS TRUE)

§ `s 302 Compromise or arrangement between corporation and creditors or stockholders`

-- The provision is in the original certificate: everyone who becomes a creditor or stockholder is bound.
#ASSERT (`s 302(a) the person is bound by the provision permitted by section 102(b)(2)` WITH `the provision permitted by § 102(b)(2) is included in the original certificate of incorporation` IS TRUE, `the date the provision was inserted in the certificate of incorporation by an amendment, if it was` IS NOTHING, `the date the person became a creditor or stockholder` IS YearMonthDay 2020 5 5) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Inserted by an amendment on 15 January 2026: bound if the person became a creditor or stockholder after the amendment.
#ASSERT (`s 302(a) the person is bound by the provision permitted by section 102(b)(2)` WITH `the provision permitted by § 102(b)(2) is included in the original certificate of incorporation` IS FALSE, `the date the provision was inserted in the certificate of incorporation by an amendment, if it was` IS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15), `the date the person became a creditor or stockholder` IS YearMonthDay 2026 1 16) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- On the day of the amendment, or before it: the text does not say, so not covered.
#ASSERT (`s 302(a) the person is bound by the provision permitted by section 102(b)(2)` WITH `the provision permitted by § 102(b)(2) is included in the original certificate of incorporation` IS FALSE, `the date the provision was inserted in the certificate of incorporation by an amendment, if it was` IS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15), `the date the person became a creditor or stockholder` IS YearMonthDay 2026 1 15) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 302(a) the person is bound by the provision permitted by section 102(b)(2)` WITH `the provision permitted by § 102(b)(2) is included in the original certificate of incorporation` IS FALSE, `the date the provision was inserted in the certificate of incorporation by an amendment, if it was` IS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15), `the date the person became a creditor or stockholder` IS YearMonthDay 2025 12 31) EQUALS NOTHING
